  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Suppose $(6a-9b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $a\\cdot a>0$\n- $a\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}(b\\cdot a)$\n- $b\\cdot a=-4$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indedd, $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Simplifying the expression $(6a-9b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a-9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (6a)\\cdot a-(9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a) & =9(b\\cdot a) \\\\ a\\cdot a & =\\frac{3}{2}(b\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=-4$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6a-9b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 6(a\\cdot a)-9(-4) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-6,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"I only\".",
